<title>UK: UK's T&amp;N extends Kolbenschmidt options.</title>
<headline>UK's T&amp;N extends Kolbenschmidt options.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>British engineering group T&amp;N Plc said on Tuesday it had extended its options over a 24.99 percent stake in German car components firm Kolbenschmidt AG until September 1997.  </p>
<p>T&amp;N also confirmed that Germany's Commerzbank AG had transferred the option arrangements to Metallbank GmbH, which was acting on behalf of a group of European investors.</p>
<p>T&amp;N said the transfer would cost it about 8.0 million stg.</p>
<p>The firm said an announcement about its options over a further 24.99 percent of Kolbenschmidt shares would be made shortly.</p>
<p>T&amp;N's shares were unchanged at 175.5p by 1350 GMT.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
